u can see a more-detailed trace of the CUDA Graph components by adding the `--cuda-graph-trace=node` option to the nsys profile command. ... And the minimal API to begin capture, end capture, then launch the captured graph.\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n1. Preparing An Application For Profiling — Profiler 12.9 documentation (https://docs.nvidia.com/cuda/profiler-users-guide/)\\nciteturn0search3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 10 months ago; GPU-Trace mode provides a timeline of all activities taking place on the GPU in chronological order. ... The number shown in the square brackets after the kernel name correlates to the CUDA API that launched that kernel.\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\\nGPU Trace UI Reference — Nsight Graphics (https://docs.nvidia.com/nsight-graphics/UserGuide/gpu-trace-ui.html)\\nciteturn0search4 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last month; When an application uses CUDA together with a graphics API such as D3D12 or Vulkan, the timeline contains separate graphics and CUDA contexts. ... The GPU Trace timeline is useful when you want to see where CUDA work occurs relative to graphics work, and whether context switches or gaps between contexts affect the frame.\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\\nNVIDIA HPC Compilers User's Guide — NVIDIA HPC Compilers User's Guide 25.1 documentation (https://docs.nvidia.com/hpc-sdk/archive/25.1/compilers/hpc-compilers-user-guide/index.html)\\nciteturn0search5 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 7 months ago; Nsight Systems Report1 Timeline ... You can see a more-detailed trace of the CUDA Graph components by adding the `--cuda-graph-trace=node` option to the nsys profile command. ... And the minimal API to begin capture, end capture, then launch the captured graph.\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\\nGPU Trace Overview — Nsight Graphics (https://docs.nvidia.com/nsight-graphics/UserGuide/gpu-trace-overview.html)\\nciteturn0search6 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last month; GPU Trace uses timestamps to construct a detailed timeline of GPU events which allows you to see for example when each draw or dispatch event occured and how long it took to complete. ... By default, GPU Trace allocates enough memory to store 100,000 timestamps per API device, which is plenty for most workloads. ... Nvidia GPUs allow GPU Trace to collect detailed metrics and warp-state data with low overhead, helping you understand how GPU hardware is utilized during a traced region.\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\\nPerformance Issues — CUDA Graph Best Practice for PyTorch (https://docs.nvidia.com/dl-cuda-graph/troubleshooting/performance-issues.html)\\nciteturn0search7 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 7 months ago; For profiling CUDA graphs specifically, use the `--cuda-graph-trace` option.The default `graph` granularity traces graphs as a whole with minimal overhead, while `node` granularity collects individual node activities but may cause significant runtime overhead.\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\\nNsight Systems :: CUDA Toolkit Documentation (https://docs.nvidia.com/cuda/nsight-systems/index.html)\\nciteturn0search8 [wordlim: 200] Published: 3.1 years ago; Crawled: 10 months ago; Nsight Systems (PDF) - v12.2.145 (older) - Last updated August 24, 2023 - Send Feedback (CUDAIssues@nvidia.com) ... NVIDIA® Nsight™ Systems provides developers a system-wide visualization of an applications performance.\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\\nAdvanced Performance Measurement Techniques — NVIDIA TensorRT (https://docs.nvidia.com/deeplearning/tensorrt/10.x.x/performance/measurement-techniques.html)\\nciteturn0search9 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 months ago;     nsys profile -o foo_profile --capture-range cudaProfilerApi --cuda-graph-trace=node trtexec --profilingVerbosity=detailed --loadEngine=foo.plan --warmUp=0 --duration=0 --iterations=50 --useCudaGraphOptional: Enable GPU Metrics Sampling in Nsight Systems\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\\nCUDA Driver API :: CUDA Toolkit Documentation (https://docs.nvidia.com/cuda/cuda-driver-api/group__CUDA__PROFILER.html)\\nciteturn0search10 [wordlim: 200] Published: 2 months ago; Crawled: 2 months ago; CUDA Driver API (PDF) - v13.3.1 (older) - Last updated June 29, 2026 - Send Feedback ... cuProfilerInitialize, cuProfilerStop, cudaProfilerStart\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\\nDLProf User Guide - NVIDIA Docs (https://docs.nvidia.com/deeplearning/frameworks/dlprof-user-guide/2111/index.html)\\nciteturn0search11 [wordlim: 200] Published: 4.8 years ago; Crawled: today; To determine the GPU time, Nsight Systems correlates all of the CUDA API calls to specific NVTX range in which they were called.\\n\"}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0a88d-678c-7661-bf44-b73f90780fbc","create_time":1789534267.2284434}}}
