o disable tracing CPU context switches. \\n116-\\t   'system-wide' requires root privileges or a paranoid level of 0 or less.\\n117-\\t   If CPU IP/backtrace sampling is enabled, --cpuctxsw equals the --sample setting.\\n118:\\t   For example, if --sample=process-tree, then --cpuctxsw=process-tree.\\n119:\\t   If --sample=none and a target application is launched, the default is 'process-tree',\\n120-\\t   otherwise the default is 'none'.\\n121-\\n122-\\t--cuda-event-trace=\\n123-\\n124-\\t   Possible values are 'auto', 'true' or 'false'.\\n125-\\t   Trace CUDA Event completion on the device side, and get better correlation\\n126-\\t   support among CUDA Event APIs. Applicable only when CUDA tracing is enabled.\\n127-\\t   Note that 'CUDA Event' refers to the synchronization mechanism (cudaEventRecord,\\n--\\n159:\\t--cuda-graph-trace=<granularity>[:<launch origin>][:<nvtx mode>]\\n160-\\n161-\\t   Set the granularity, launch origin, and NVTX projection mode for CUDA graph trace.\\n162-\\t   Applicable only when CUDA tracing is enabled.\\n163-\\t   Optional modifiers can appear in any order after the granularity.\\n164-\\n165-\\t   Possible values for <granularity> are 'graph' or 'node'.\\n166-\\t   If 'graph' is selected, CUDA graphs will be traced as a whole and node\\n167-\\t   activities will not be collected. This can reduce overhead to the minimal,\\n--\\n178:\\t   version 13.0 or higher, and '--trace=cuda' must be enabled without '--trace=cuda-sw'.\\n179-\\t   This may cause significant runtime overhead.\\n180-\\t   If granularity is set to 'graph' and the CUDA driver version is 12.3 or higher,\\n181-\\t   the default is 'host-and-device'. For 'node', the default is 'host-only' unless \\n182-\\t   hardware trace is enabled and the CUDA driver version is 13.0 or higher.\\n183-\\n184-\\t   Possible values for <nvtx mode> are 'nvtx-live' or 'nvtx-precapture'.\\n185-\\t   Controls how NVTX projection works for CUDA Graph nodes.\\n186-\\t   'nvtx-live': NVTX projection is available for graphs constructed while\\n--\\n190:\\t   before collection begins (e.g., with --capture-range=cudaProfilerApi).\\n191-\\t   This adds overhead during graph construction and increases memory usage.\\n192-\\t   Requires granularity 'node', CUDA tracing (-t cuda), and NVTX tracing\\n193-\\t   (-t nvtx). Experimental.\\n194-\\t   Default is 'nvtx-live'.\\n195-\\n196-\\t   Application scope.\\n197-\\n198-\\t--cuda-memory-usage=\\n--\\n264:            Implies '--trace=nvtx'.\\n265-\\n266-\\t--debug-symbols=\\n267-\\n268-\\t   Specify the paths to directories with symbol files.\\n269-\\t   Multiple directories can be selected, separated by a colon (':') only (no spaces).\\n270-\\n271-\\t--discard-environment=\\n272-\\n--\\n431:\\t   Note that this switch is applicable only when --capture-range=hotkey is specified.\\n432-\\t   Default is `F12`.\\n433-\\n434-\\t--ib-net-info-devices=\\n435-\\n436-           A comma-separated list of NICs names.\\n437-           The NICs which ibdiagnet will use for networks discovery.\\n438-           This option creates the ibdiagnet files to be used for\\n439-           collecting network information.\\n--\\n517:\\t--kill=\\n518-\\n519-\\t   Possible values are 'none', 'sigkill', 'sigterm', or signal number.\\n520-\\t   Send signal to the target application's process group when ending/shutting down profiling session.\\n521-\\t   Default is 'sigterm', so the application is terminated when profiling session ends/is shutdown.\\n522-\\n523-\\t--mpi-impl=\\n524-\\n525-\\t   Possible values are 'openmpi' or 'mpich'.\\n--\\n528:\\t   Note that this switch is applicable only when --trace=mpi is specified.\\n529-\\t   If no MPI implementation is specified, nsys tries to automatically detect it based on the\\n530-\\t   dynamic linker's search path. If this fails, 'openmpi' is used.\\n531-\\n532-\\t-n, --inherit-environment=\\n533-\\n534-\\t   Possible values are 'true' or 'false'.\\n535-\\t   Inherit environment variables.\\n536-\\t   Default is 'true'.\\n--\\n566:\\t   Note that both switches are applicable only when --trace=nvtx is specified.\\n567-\\n568-\\t-o, --output=\\n569-\\n570-\\t   Output report filename.\\n571-\\t   Any %q{ENV_VAR} pattern in the filename will be substituted with the value of the \\n572-\\t   environment variable.\\n573-\\t   Any %h pattern in the filename will be substituted with the hostname of the system.\\n574-\\t   Any %p pattern in the filename will be substituted with the PID of the target process or\\n--\\n585:\\t   Note that this switch is applicable only when --trace=opengl is specified.\\n586-\\t   Default is 'true'. Application scope.\\n587-\\n\"}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0a88d-678c-7661-bf44-b73f90780fbc","create_time":1789534309.7994778}}}
